  <prov:used rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/vgo_prov#ProposedAxioms"/>
  <prov:used rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/vgo_prov#ProposedTests"/>
  <prov:generated rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/vgo_prov#OntologyDraft_iteration0"/>
  <prov:wasInformedBy rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/vgo_prov#TestGenerationActivity"/>
  <prov:wasAssociatedWith rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/vgo_prov#agent_OntoGeneration_Agent"/>
  <prov:hadRole rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/vgo_prov#GeneratorRole"/>
  <prov:hadPlan rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/vgo_prov#GenerationPrompt"/>
  <prov:qualifiedAssociation>
    <prov:Association>
      <prov:agent rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/vgo_prov#agent_OntoGeneration_Agent"/>
      <prov:hadRole rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/vgo_prov#GeneratorRole"/>
    </prov:Association>
  </prov:qualifiedAssociation>
  <vaem:rationale>The ontology models classes and properties extracted from the competency questions' terms to answer each atomic question. Classes represent entities like Player, Game, Achievement, etc. Object properties link these classes according to the relations queried, and datatype properties capture attributes like username, hoursPlayed, and releaseDate. Domains and ranges are assigned based on the supplied terms and proposed axioms, with functional characteristics applied to data properties. Axioms explicitly state domain and range constraints to satisfy validation tests.</vaem:rationale>
</prov:Activity>

